DOC|subsystem_reading|v1|updated=2026-04-10c
META|inertia=LOW|parent=architecture_root.dsb
META|files=tools/ebook_reader.py,tools/training.py,tools/reading_integration.py,tools/learner.py,cognition/word_graph.py,claudecode/book_learner.py
META|purpose=book reading → graph training → realtime discussion

DESIGN_POINTS|
  DP1|reading pipeline: open_book→read_chunk→extract→stew(TWM)→NE integrates→LTM
  DP2|stew salience=0.65 (above NE force-run threshold 0.60); guarantees NE processes book content; kwarg=content_csb= (G-OVN-2: was content=, causing 799 silent failures)
  DP3|G54 extraction gate: IGOR_READING_EXTRACT=true; reads trigger interpretive edge creation
  DP4|training corpus: staged ~/.TheIgors/training_corpus/; fetch→train→evict; cursor=index.json
  DP5|word graph trained from book text: enriches predict_next() + habit pattern matching
  DP6|CIFS stale handle: _local_copy() copies to /tmp before read; transparent to caller
  DP7|cloud_ok per-chunk (D071): book_learner._should_use_local() reads ~/.TheIgors/cloud_ok_override.json each chunk; mode can change mid-book without restart; --local flag still forces local
  DP8|deposition vs encoding (D170): READ_* nodes from raw extraction are deposition only; encoding requires the 5-step integration pipeline (embed+link+spine+interp+arousal)
  DP9|drain runner path fix (D181): cron was using IGOR_INSTANCE_ID=Igor-wild-0001 (wrong case) → empty queue for weeks; fixed to Igor-wild-0001; 146 items now draining
  DP10|D333 situated-reading pass-2: book_learner --pass2 uses _EXTRACT_PROMPT_PASS2 with dynamic context injection (watch-list goals, hot attractors, open gaps) + practitioner questions (relevance/levers/mechanisms/contradictions). Result: 1,078 situated nodes vs 4 generic nodes per book (270× improvement). Nodes tagged with metadata[pass]=2, extraction_type, relevance.
  DP11|multi-instance reading safety: feed_reading_list() uses atomic UPDATE...RETURNING claim-and-fetch in single DB transaction; prevents race where two instances both SELECT same pending book before claiming. Applies to all multi-instance Igor deployments.

READING_INTEGRATION_PIPELINE|
  purpose=second-pass integration after book_learner deposits READ_* nodes
  steps=1.embed (nomic-embed-text) → 2.link (cosine+BFS to existing nodes) → 3.spine (narrative thread) → 4.interp (interpretive edges from salient pairs) → 5.arousal (valence/arousal/dominance)
  tool=integrate_reading(book, batch=200) in tools/reading_integration.py
  backfill=claudecode/reading_integrator.py — one-time backfill of already-deposited nodes
  deposit_primitive=_deposit_nodes() in cortex.py — canonical write path for all book nodes
  book_learner=now runs 5-step pipeline inline; new books encoded on deposit
  experiment_roadmap=D179: 8 experiments; 1-5 done (pipeline built+validated); 6=bulk reading running (146 items); 7=swarm; 8=capacity
  reading_speed=#300: IGOR_READING_SPEED_SPS configurable (default 1 sentence/sec; not yet implemented)

EBOOK_READER|
  calibre=~/.TheIgors/akien/onedrive/AkiensMedia/Ebooks/Calibre Portable/Calibre Library
  loaded_books=Damasio ids 3023(Feeling of What Happens),3300(Self Comes to Mind),3032(Descartes Error),3025(Looking for Spinoza),3026(Strange Order of Things)
  formats=epub,mobi,azw,pdf|nltk sentence tokenization
  state=reading_state.json|tracks position per session
  tools=find_book,open_book,read_chunk,jump_to_chapter,reading_position,list_reading_sessions

TRAINING_CORPUS|
  path=~/.TheIgors/training_corpus/
  cap=IGOR_TRAINING_MAX_CHARS (1MB default; was IGOR_TRAINING_MAX_PARAS=800)
  flow=fetch URL→store→train word_graph→evict when complete/disk_tight
  eviction_priority=complete first, in_progress second (cursor checkpointed), pending last (re-fetchable)
  local_source=~/TheIgorsProject/ (Akien's writings)
  gutenberg_list=~/TheIgorsProject/akien/Readings/gutenberg.org_top_100_vocabulary_expanding_books.txt

MILESTONE|books_realtime
  definition=Igor discusses book content from graph memory without being prompted
  why_matters=confirms read→extract→graph→respond loop working end-to-end
  gates=Claude training run (don't train until this works; else reinforce incomplete behavior)

BOOK_LEARNER_OBSERVABILITY|
  console_note=open_book() prints "★ Opening" or "▶ Resuming" to stdout on every open
  absorption_note=book_learner.py prints new/resume + checkpoint stats after loading progress
  log=subprocess stdout routed to ~/.TheIgors/logs/book_learner.log (was DEVNULL); tailable

READING_LIST_STATUS|G-RL3: drain_learn_queue.py sets status=in_progress+started_at on calibre launch; book_learner.py sets status=completed+completed_at on full run (position>=total_sentences, no --limit)

DECISIONS|D038,D052,D071,D170,D173,D179,D181
KNOWN_FAILURES|F001(OOM from word_graph JSON — fixed by SQLite migration),F012(stale-CIFS)
OPEN_TICKETS|#300(reading speed configurable — IGOR_READING_SPEED_SPS)
